{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013vx4457dusMXiuMQXBe4RS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd046-nproc\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/nproc: Print Number of Available Processing Units\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Build scripts and parallel job schedulers use nproc to determine the number of available\n6\t  CPUs for concurrency decisions (e.g., make -j$(nproc)). The utility supports an --all flag\n7\t  for installed processors and an --ignore=N flag to reserve cores. The Go implementation must\n8\t  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gnproc, installed by coreutils) on stdout and exit\n9\t  code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the number of available processing units.\n13\t  - G2: Support --all and --ignore=N flags for installed count and core reservation.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior and flags\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the number of available processing units followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"--all must print the number of installed processors, which may differ from the available count if CPU affinity or cgroups restrict the set.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"--ignore=N must subtract N from the processor count and print the result. The result must never be less than 1.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: --all and --ignore=N may be combined. When combined, --ignore subtracts from the installed count.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Error handling\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: If any positional operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: If --ignore is given a non-numeric value, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n37\t\n38\t  R3:\n39\t    title: Differential testing\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R3.1:\n42\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gnproc) via pkg/testutils.\n43\t      - R3.2:\n44\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default invocation, --all, --ignore=1, --all --ignore=1, and error cases.\"\n45\t      - R3.3:\n46\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n47\t\n48\tnon_goals:\n49\t  - cmd/nproc does not set CPU affinity or modify scheduling.\n50\t  - cmd/nproc does not read cgroup limits on macOS; the available and installed counts may be identical.\n51\t\n52\tacceptance_criteria:\n53\t  - id: AC1\n54\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/nproc prints the CPU count, matching gnproc.\"\n55\t    traces:\n56\t      - R1.1\n57\t      - R1.2\n58\t      - R1.3\n59\t      - R1.4\n60\t  - id: AC2\n61\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/nproc --ignore=1 prints one fewer than the default, matching gnproc.\"\n62\t    traces:\n63\t      - R1.3\n64\t      - R1.4\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t      - R3.2\n67\t  - id: AC3\n68\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gnproc passes for all supported flags and error cases.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R1.2\n71\t      - R2.1\n72\t      - R2.2\n73\t      - R2.3\n74\t      - R3.1\n75\t      - R3.2\n76\t      - R3.3\n77\t  - id: AC4\n78\t    criterion: \"cmd/nproc compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R1.3\n83\t      - R1.4\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R2.3\n87\t      - R3.1\n88\t      - R3.2\n89\t      - R3.3\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ebd210b-4c2b-4e3c-bd51-318709e17a48","uuid":"69ca1289-708e-4073-86df-65e8660f8556","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:22:15.548Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5193/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml","content":"id: srd046-nproc\ntitle: \"cmd/nproc: Print Number of Available Processing Units\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Build scripts and parallel job schedulers use nproc to determine the number of available\n  CPUs for concurrency decisions (e.g., make -j$(nproc)). The utility supports an --all flag\n  for installed processors and an --ignore=N flag to reserve cores. The Go implementation must\n  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gnproc, installed by coreutils) on stdout and exit\n  code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the number of available processing units.\n  - G2: Support --all and --ignore=N flags for installed count and core reservation.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and flags\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the number of available processing units followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"--all must print the number of installed processors, which may differ from the available count if CPU affinity or cgroups restrict the set.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"--ignore=N must subtract N from the processor count and print the result. The result must never be less than 1.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: --all and --ignore=N may be combined. When combined, --ignore subtracts from the installed count.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any positional operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: If --ignore is given a non-numeric value, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gnproc) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: default invocation, --all, --ignore=1, --all --ignore=1, and error cases.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/nproc does not set CPU affinity or modify scheduling.\n  - cmd/nproc does not read cgroup limits on macOS; the available and installed counts may be identical.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/nproc prints the CPU count, matching gnproc.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/nproc --ignore=1 prints one fewer than the default, matching gnproc.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gnproc passes for all supported flags and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/nproc compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
