{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a detailed stitch task (#5193) to create differential tests for `cmd/nproc` implementing srd046-nproc requirements R3.1, R3.2, and R3.3. The task requires creating a single file `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go` that uses the project's `pkg/testutils` differential testing framework to compare the Go nproc binary against the Homebrew GNU reference binary `gnproc`. The tests must cover default invocation, --all, --ignore=1, --all --ignore=1, and error cases, with LC_ALL=C set in the environment.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gnproc)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `testutils.DiffTest` struct for test harness\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gnproc\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful degradation\n   - LC_ALL=C environment setting (handled automatically by testutils.buildEnv)\n   - The nproc utility prints CPU count, supports --all and --ignore=N flags\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - SPDX copyright header requirement on all Go files\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml`\n     - SRD defining all requirements for nproc. R3.1-R3.3 are the differential testing requirements being implemented.\n     - R3.1: Tests must compare stdout and exit codes via pkg/testutils\n     - R3.2: Must cover default, --all, --ignore=1, --all --ignore=1, error cases\n     - R3.3: All tests must set LC_ALL=C\n\n   - `cmd/nproc/main.go` (existing, complete implementation)\n     - Implements R1.1-R1.4 and R2.1-R2.3\n     - Key: `allFlag` is captured but unused (`_ = allFlag`), so --all behaves same as default on macOS\n     - Uses `runtime.NumCPU()` for processor count\n     - `parseIgnore` helper rejects negative values and non-numeric input\n     - Error messages follow pattern: `nproc: <error>\\nTry 'nproc --help' for more information.`\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     // Implements srd046-nproc R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3.\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"runtime\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         allFlag := false\n         ignoreN := 0\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         for len(args) > 0 {\n             arg := args[0]\n             args = args[1:]\n             if arg == \"--\" { break }\n             if arg == \"--all\" { allFlag = true; continue }\n             if arg == \"--ignore\" {\n                 if len(args) == 0 {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: option '--ignore' requires an argument\\n\")\n                     fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 if !parseIgnore(args[0], &ignoreN) { os.Exit(1) }\n                 args = args[1:]\n                 continue\n             }\n             if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--ignore=\") {\n                 val := arg[len(\"--ignore=\"):]\n                 if !parseIgnore(val, &ignoreN) { os.Exit(1) }\n                 continue\n             }\n             if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1 {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: extra operand '%s'\\n\", arg)\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: extra operand '%s'\\n\", arg)\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'nproc --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         count := runtime.NumCPU()\n         _ = allFlag\n         count -= ignoreN\n         if count < 1 { count = 1 }\n         if _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, count); err != nil { os.Exit(1) }\n     }\n     func parseIgnore(val string, n *int) bool {\n         v, err := strconv.Atoi(val)\n         if err != nil || v < 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"nproc: invalid number: '%s'\\n\", val)\n             return false\n         }\n         *n = v\n         return true\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - Provides `DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs each test as a named subtest\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the binary (defined in build.go, not shown but referenced)\n     - `buildEnv` automatically sets LC_ALL=C (satisfying R3.3)\n\n   - `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go` (to be created)\n     - This is the file that needs to be written\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only two Read operations were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand R3.1-R3.3 requirements for differential testing\n   - Read the existing main.go to understand what flags and error cases exist and need test coverage\n   - Identified the test cases needed per R3.2: default, --all, --ignore=1, --all --ignore=1, error cases (extra operand, non-numeric --ignore, unknown flag)\n   - Noted that ExitCode field defaults to 0 in DiffTest, so error cases need ExitCode: 1\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely long task description with role, repository_files, project_context, execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. Core request: implement srd046-nproc R3.1-R3.3 by creating `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go`.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go` with differential tests following the project pattern\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/nproc/` to verify no issues (AC4)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/nproc/... -count=1` to verify tests compile and run (AC1)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two key files needed to implement the task:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml` (the SRD with R3.1-R3.3 requirements)\n   - `cmd/nproc/main.go` (the existing implementation to understand what to test)\n   \n   I was about to create `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go` with the following planned test cases based on R3.2:\n   - \"default\" (no args, ExitCode 0)\n   - \"--all\" (ExitCode 0)\n   - \"--ignore=1\" (ExitCode 0)\n   - \"--all --ignore=1\" (ExitCode 0)\n   - \"extra operand\" (positional arg like \"foo\", ExitCode 1)\n   - \"non-numeric ignore\" (--ignore=abc, ExitCode 1)\n   - \"unknown flag\" (--bogus, ExitCode 1)\n\n   The test file must follow the exact differential testing pattern from shared_protocols with copyright header, BuildBinary, LookPath for gnproc, t.Skip if not found, and RunDiffTests.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go` using the Write tool with the complete test file implementing the differential testing pattern. The file should include:\n   - SPDX copyright header\n   - Package main with imports for testing, os/exec, and testutils\n   - TestDiff function using `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gnproc\")`\n   - t.Skip when gnproc is not found\n   - DiffTest slice covering all cases from R3.2\n   - Call to `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   \n   Then verify with `go vet ./cmd/nproc/` and `go test ./cmd/nproc/... -count=1`.\n\n   This directly corresponds to the task description: \"files: path: cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go, action: create, note: Differential tests comparing Go nproc binary against gnproc reference binary\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5193/6ebd210b-4c2b-4e3c-bd51-318709e17a48.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ebd210b-4c2b-4e3c-bd51-318709e17a48","uuid":"fb7d5cb1-f82a-4539-b876-702689906030","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:23:22.015Z","isSynthetic":true}
